        injectionType: "Multi-Point Manifold Injection / Bosch LH-Jetronic (Relies on mass airflow sensing. The most critical flaw of this era is the infamous 'biodegradable' engine wiring harness. Between 1992 and 1996, Mercedes used eco-friendly insulation that crumbles to dust under hood heat, causing massive short circuits that fry the extremely expensive ECU and EZL ignition modules.)",
        engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ miles (The M119 5.0L is universally regarded as one of the best V8 engines Mercedes-Benz ever engineered. The closed-deck aluminum block and forged internals are virtually bulletproof. However, its survival depends entirely on replacing the biodegradable wiring harness, the plastic upper timing chain guides, and the plastic upper oil tube seals. If these age-related flaws are addressed, the block will outlast the chassis.)",
