        timingType: "Double-roller chain (The massive dual-row timing chain is robust, but the incredible heat generated by the V12 turns the upper plastic guide rails extremely brittle. If these guides snap, pieces fall into the timing cover, causing the chain to skip teeth and resulting in catastrophic destruction of the 48-valve head. Preventative replacement of these guides at 150,000 km is absolutely critical.)",
        injectionType: "Multi-Point Manifold Injection / Bosch ME-Motronic (Later facelift models transitioned to the vastly superior ME-Motronic system. It replaced the dual distributors and fragile EZL ignition modules with a modern distributorless ignition system using individual coil packs. The biodegradable wiring harness issue was mostly resolved for these late ME-Motronic cars.)",
        engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ km (The M120 V12 is a monumental engineering achievement. Mechanically, the closed-deck aluminum block and forged internals are virtually indestructible, capable of massive mileage. However, the lifespan is dictated entirely by its horrifying electrical complexity and heat management. If the plastic upper timing chain guides and the plastic upper oil tube seals are replaced preventatively, the block will easily outlast the chassis.)",
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated",
        ecuType: "Bosch ME 1.0 (A massive upgrade over the early models. This modern Engine Control Unit integrates ignition and fueling seamlessly, eliminating the incredibly expensive and rare EZL module entirely. Tuning potential is slightly better than early models, but still limited due to being naturally aspirated.)",
        euroStandard: "Euro 2",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "800+ hp (The M120 6.0L block is a legend. The internal rotating assembly is so strong and overbuilt that this exact architecture formed the basis for the Pagani Zonda hypercar engine. The stock internals can handle twin-turbo setups effortlessly, though the transmission cannot handle massive torque spikes.)",
