        injectionType: "Multi-Point Manifold Injection / Bosch ME-Motronic (AMG-tuned for massive flow rates and aggressive timing curves to support the 7.0L displacement. These engines use a highly complex dual-ECU setup. The wiring harnesses in these late-model AMG builds are generally more durable than early 90s units, but the sheer heat output of the 7.0L engine continues to stress all under-hood rubber and electrical components.)",
        engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km (The AMG 7.0L M120 is a rare, hand-built masterpiece. The closed-deck aluminum block and forged internals are incredibly robust, forming the basis for the Pagani Zonda engine. However, its lifespan is entirely dictated by its immense heat output and electrical complexity. If the plastic timing guides are replaced and the cooling system is maintained perfectly, the engine is capable of very high mileage.)",
