        timingType: "Double-roller chain (The massive dual-row timing chain is robust, but the extreme heat generated by the 7.3L AMG displacement turns the upper plastic guide rails extremely brittle. If these guides snap, pieces fall into the timing cover, causing the chain to skip teeth and resulting in catastrophic destruction of the 48-valve head. Preventative replacement of these guides at 100,000 km is absolutely critical.)",
        injectionType: "Multi-Point Manifold Injection / Bosch ME-Motronic (AMG-tuned for massive flow rates and aggressive timing curves to support the 7.3L displacement. This late version uses individual coil packs, which is a significant reliability improvement over early 90s dual-distributor systems, but the wiring and heat management remain incredibly complex.)",
        engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km (The M120 7.3L AMG is perhaps the most exclusive V12 ever produced by Mercedes. Mechanically, the closed-deck aluminum block and custom forged internals are robust. However, because these were hand-built and heavily modified, the lifespan depends entirely on the quality of the internal assembly and the rigor of the maintenance performed. Excessive heat buildup in the tight C140 engine bay is the primary limiting factor for longevity.)",
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated",
