        injectionType: "Multi-Point Injection / Bosch Motronic ME 2.8 (A very robust and simple injection system. It uses 16 spark plugs—two per cylinder—for complete combustion. The US-market version features more restrictive catalytic converters and slightly altered fueling maps to meet strict LEV/ULEV emissions standards.)",
        engineLifespan: "250 000 - 350 000+ miles (The M113 is widely considered one of the most reliable V8 engines ever built by Mercedes-Benz. It features a simplified 3-valve-per-cylinder design, reducing moving parts. The block is robust and the engine rarely dies from mechanical failure; it usually survives until the chassis rusts or the ABC suspension becomes too expensive to fix.)",
