          "Active Body Control (ABC) Pump & Strut Failure: The high-pressure hydraulic suspension pump is highly prone to failure. Struts leak and valve blocks clog, causing the car to collapse to the ground.",
          "Engine Mount Collapse: The gargantuan weight of the V12 engine, combined with 800 Nm of twisting torque, absolutely obliterates engine and transmission mounts, causing terrible cabin vibrations.",
          "Intercooler Pump Failure: The factory Bosch intercooler pump frequently fails, causing the intake charge to overheat and the ECU to drastically pull engine power (heat soak).",
          "722.6 Conductor Plate Failure: The transmission speed sensors fail, triggering Limp Mode and locking the transmission in 2nd gear."
