        yearRange: "1999-2002",
        timingType: "Single-roller chain. The M113 5.4-liter AMG variant utilizes a highly dependable single-roller timing chain that is universally praised for its durability. Unlike older V8s, it does not suffer from catastrophically brittle plastic guide rails. The timing chain mechanism is generally considered bulletproof for the life of the engine, though replacing the chain tensioner preventatively at high mileage is a sound practice to prevent timing chain slap on cold startups.",
        injectionType: "Multi-Point Manifold Injection / Bosch Motronic ME 2.8. A brilliantly simple and robust sequential fuel injection system. It avoids the immense complexity and carbon-buildup issues of modern direct injection. This engine utilizes a unique twin-spark ignition setup, meaning it requires 16 spark plugs to ensure a complete, efficient burn inside the cylinder. While this makes spark plug replacement slightly more expensive, the individual coil packs are infinitely more reliable than the disastrous coil cassettes used on the V12 models.",
        engineLifespan: "350 000 - 500 000+ km. This naturally aspirated 5.4L AMG engine is famously one of the most durable and trouble-free powerplants to ever emerge from Affalterbach. Without the added thermal stress and mechanical complexity of the later supercharged variants (the M113K) or the terrifying electronics of the V12 models, this engine regularly exceeds massive mileages. As long as basic oil changes are performed and minor leaks are addressed, the engine block will easily outlast the chassis it sits in.",
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated. Free from the complex superchargers, intercoolers, and secondary water pumps that complicate the later CL 55 AMG models. This ensures a highly linear, immediate throttle response and drastically lower under-hood temperatures, significantly prolonging the life of rubber seals and wiring harnesses.",
        ecuType: "Bosch Motronic ME 2.8. A highly reliable engine control unit that rarely suffers from internal hardware failures. Because this is a naturally aspirated engine tuned by AMG from the factory, aftermarket tuning potential via software flashes is extremely minimal. The ECU optimally manages the aggressive AMG camshaft profiles and fueling curves.",
        euroStandard: "Euro 3",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "500+ hp. The internal components, particularly the forged crankshaft and robust pistons chosen by AMG, are incredibly strong. Many enthusiasts have successfully bolted aftermarket superchargers onto this naturally aspirated block with great success, though the factory naturally aspirated setup provides the purest reliability.",
