          "Economic Total Loss (ABC Suspension): A catastrophic failure of the ABC hydraulic pump can contaminate the entire system with metal shavings, necessitating a full-system flush and replacement of all components, which often exceeds the car's resale value.",
          "Catastrophic Engine Failure (Detonation): If the intercooler pump fails or low-octane fuel is used, the supercharged engine is highly prone to detonation (knock). This can instantly crack ring lands or destroy pistons if the ECU safety protocols do not react fast enough.",
          "Drivetrain Stress: The sheer force of the 700 Nm torque output regularly snaps flex discs, destroys engine mounts, and strips the splines in the driveshaft, leading to expensive driveline repairs.",
