        timingType: "Double-roller chain. The M275 V12 features a massive, heavy-duty double-roller timing chain, similar to the CL 600. It is extremely robust, but the extreme, inescapable thermal load generated by the 6.0L BiTurbo engine eventually bakes the plastic timing chain guide rails until they are brittle. If these guides snap, pieces can jam the chain, potentially causing a catastrophic timing skip and total engine destruction. Preventative inspection and replacement of these guides at 150,000 km is absolutely mandatory, though the labor cost is enormous due to the engine size and complexity.",
        injectionType: "Multi-Point Injection / Bosch ME 2.7.2. This system is exceptionally complex, managing 24 spark plugs via dual ignition coil cassettes spanning the entire length of each cylinder bank. These cassettes are fed by a central voltage transformer, and the entire system is highly sensitive to heat and voltage fluctuations. The direct fuel injection system operates at high pressures, relying on a dedicated high-pressure fuel system to manage the massive fueling requirements of a 612 hp V12 engine.",
        engineLifespan: "200 000 - 300 000+ km. The M275 6.0L BiTurbo is a mechanical masterpiece, but it is effectively the limit of how much power can be safely extracted from an engine block that is also responsible for managing extreme heat. The forged internals are massively over-engineered. However, the lifespan is entirely dependent on the owner's willingness to replace aging rubber cooling lines, fragile plastic components, and the astronomical cost of replacing failing ignition electronics. Neglect leads to engine death via heat soak or fuel system failure.",
        turboType: "Twin-Turbocharged. Features two water-cooled turbochargers integrated closely to the exhaust manifolds, delivering a massive, unstoppable wave of 1,000 Nm of torque. The intense heat created in the V-valley creates a hostile environment for the plastic turbo coolant lines, which are guaranteed to crack and leak. The turbos themselves are robust, but they require pristine oil change intervals and cool-down periods to survive high mileage.",
        ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.7.2. An exceptionally advanced unit, this ECU manages the complex twin-turbo system, variable valve timing, and electronic throttle bodies. It is uniquely tuned for the 65 AMG and represents the absolute peak of V12 engine management for the era. Tuning via ECU software is extremely popular, often allowing the engine to produce well beyond the factory 1,000 Nm limit, though the transmission is rarely happy with such power.",
        euroStandard: "Euro 4",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "800+ hp. The internal rotating assembly, consisting of forged connecting rods and pistons, is incredibly stout. It is the same foundational architecture used in the Pagani Zonda. While the block can handle massive power, the 5-speed transmission is the absolute bottleneck and will fail if pushed too far beyond stock specifications.",
