    compression: "10.0:1",
    yearRange: "2010-2014",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The M157 engine family shares its core architecture with the M278 and similarly suffers from infamous timing chain tensioner issues caused by oil drain-back. Upon cold start, a distinct rattling noise indicates that the secondary chain tensioners lack oil pressure. Mercedes issued a critical service bulletin to install oil check valves behind the tensioners; if this is ignored, the chain will stretch, slap against the aluminum housing, and destroy the variable valve timing (VVT) phasers, inevitably leading to catastrophic engine failure.",
    injectionType: "Gasoline Direct Injection (GDI) / Bosch MED 17.7.3. This highly advanced system utilizes high-pressure piezoelectric injectors that spray fuel directly into the combustion chamber to maximize explosive power and efficiency. However, it relies heavily on complex mechanical high-pressure fuel pumps (HPFP) that are known to fail over time, leaving drivers stranded with severe hesitation. Furthermore, because fuel no longer washes over the intake valves, the M157 is prone to carbon buildup, which can severely restrict airflow and cause performance degradation at higher mileages.",
    engineLifespan: "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The M157 is a phenomenally powerful but highly sensitive engine due to its 'Silitec' cylinder wall scoring vulnerability. The incredibly tight engine tolerances, combined with the extreme heat from direct injection and potential injector failures, can cause the piston rings to aggressively gouge the aluminum cylinder walls. The AMG Performance Package (PP) pushes the engine significantly harder, generating more heat and cylinder pressure, which theoretically increases the risk of this scoring. Once scoring occurs, the engine consumes massive amounts of oil, loses compression, and requires a total rebuild or block replacement.",
    turboType: "Twin-Turbocharged. Features two Garrett turbochargers integrated closely to the engine block. The AMG Performance Package increases peak boost pressure from the standard 1.0 bar to 1.3 bar, significantly raising under-hood temperatures. Unfortunately, the plastic coolant lines feeding these turbos become extremely brittle from this intense V-valley heat and are absolutely guaranteed to crack over time. When these lines snap, they dump the entire coolant volume rapidly, which will warp the aluminum cylinder heads if the driver does not pull over immediately.",
    ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.3. A highly advanced Engine Control Unit that expertly manages the direct injection fueling, aggressive variable valve timing, and the elevated twin-turbo boost levels of the Performance Package. The ECU is incredibly robust and serves as an absolute tuner's dream. Even with the factory Performance Package, a Stage 1 software flash can safely unlock further massive power gains, bypassing the factory boost limits and easily pushing the vehicle past 620 horsepower.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "750+ hp. The internal components, particularly the forged connecting rods and pistons, are incredibly strong and fully capable of supporting much higher power levels than the stock 571 hp. However, drastically increasing boost pressure significantly exacerbates the risk of the dreaded cylinder wall scoring. Professional tuning is absolutely required to manage combustion temperatures carefully and prevent catastrophic internal melting.",
    fuelConsumption: {
      city: "14.5 - 17.0 L/100km",
      highway: "9.0 - 11.0 L/100km",
      mixed: "11.0 - 13.0 L/100km",
      sporty: "24.0+ L/100km"
    },
    oilSpecification: "8.5L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5 strictly required). Frequent oil changes strictly every 8,000 km are the absolute most vital preventative maintenance required to mitigate the risk of Silitec cylinder scoring. Fresh, high-quality oil is also critical to protect the delicate VVT phasers and ensure the turbocharger bearings are properly lubricated under the extreme thermal loads generated by the 1.3 bar boost pressure.",
    commonIssues: [
      "Silitec Cylinder Wall Scoring: This is the most fatal flaw of the M157 engine. A heavy knocking sound accompanied by high oil consumption indicates deeply gouged cylinder walls caused by piston ring friction. This necessitates an engine-out teardown and custom iron-sleeving to repair, which often costs more than the car is worth.",
      "Timing Chain Tensioner Rattle: A distinct rattling on cold start is caused by oil draining away from the timing chain tensioners overnight. It is absolutely critical to install updated check valves and new tensioners immediately upon noticing this sound. Failure to do so will result in a stretched timing chain and completely destroyed VVT gears.",
      "Turbo Coolant Line Failure: The factory plastic coolant lines feeding the twin turbochargers become heat-cycled and incredibly brittle over time. They tend to snap unexpectedly, dumping the entire coolant volume onto the hot exhaust. This can instantly warp the aluminum cylinder heads if the engine is not shut down within seconds.",
      "Oil Intrusion into ECU: The camshaft position sensors and magnets frequently develop internal leaks, allowing engine oil to seep out. Capillary action forces this oil to travel through the electrical wiring harness directly into the Engine Control Unit (ECU), where it shorts out the motherboard and destroys the module.",
      "MCT Transmission Judder: The 7-speed MCT transmission uses a wet startup clutch instead of a traditional torque converter. As the clutch packs wear from managing 900 Nm of torque, or the adaptation data drifts, the transmission can develop a severe judder or hesitation when pulling away from a stop. This requires frequent fluid changes and software re-adaptations.",
      "ABC Hydraulic Suspension Failure: The CL 63 relies entirely on the Active Body Control (ABC) system to manage its massive weight. The high-pressure hydraulic pump, struts, and valve blocks are extremely prone to internal seal failures and leaks. Repairing these components costs thousands of euros and is a constant maintenance battle."
    ],
    vulnerabilities: [
      "Economic Total Loss due to Cylinder Scoring: The cost of repairing M157 cylinder wall scoring is astronomically prohibitive. Engine removal, complete teardown, and custom iron sleeving routinely exceed the resale value of the car, forcing owners to either sell the car for scrap or part it out.",
      "Catastrophic Timing Chain Skip: Ignoring the cold-start rattle will eventually lead to the chain stretching and slapping violently against the timing cover. This will inevitably result in skipped timing and smashed valves, utterly destroying the 32-valve cylinder head beyond repair.",
      "ECU Destruction via Oil Wicking: If engine oil from leaking camshaft sensors travels through the wiring harness into the ECU, the electrical damage is immense and irreversible. Prevention strictly requires installing OEM sacrificial 'pigtail' extension harnesses on all camshaft sensors to block the oil path physically.",
      "Turbo Coolant Line Rupture: The sudden rupture of brittle plastic coolant lines creates an immediate, life-threatening emergency for the engine. If the driver attempts to drive even a short distance while the engine is rapidly losing coolant, the cylinder heads will warp, leading to a permanent total engine failure.",
      "Suspension Collapse (ABC): Total failure of the ABC hydraulic pump can cause metal debris to circulate throughout the high-pressure system. This results in a multi-thousand-euro suspension rebuild, ruins valve blocks, and leaves the car completely collapsed and undriveable."
    ],
