      timingType: "Chain-driven DOHC timing system with front-engine packaging. The arrangement is fundamentally robust when lubrication quality is kept high, but it is not immune to neglect. Long service intervals, contaminated oil, and frequent short-trip use accelerate tensioner wear and chain stretch. That turns a minor cold-start noise into timing deviation, rough running, and expensive top-end work if diagnosis is delayed.",
  
      injectionType: "Turbocharged gasoline direct injection. The system allows the 1.6-liter M270 to produce diesel-like low-end torque for its class while maintaining compact packaging and competitive fuel economy. As with any GDI engine, the trade-off is progressive carbon buildup on the intake valves because fuel never washes them clean. This makes PCV health, oil quality, and periodic intake cleaning central to long-term smoothness and efficiency.",
  
      engineLifespan: "Expected service life is broadly the same as the 156 hp EU-rated version because the hardware is effectively the same engine in a different measurement context. Real-world longevity depends primarily on oil change discipline, intake cleanliness, cooling reliability, and how quickly chain noise or small leaks are addressed. With good care, 220,000-320,000+ km is achievable; with neglect, medium-cost failures arrive much earlier.",
  
      turboType: "Single turbocharged 1.6-liter layout with intercooling and strong low-rpm boost strategy. The driving character is centered on usable midrange rather than high-rpm drama, which suits the CLA's daily-road mission. Turbo reliability is mostly an oil and heat-management story, so old oil, crankcase ventilation issues, and ignored intake leaks remain the main threats.",
  
      ecuType: "Bosch MED17-series management calibrated to market-specific measurement and emissions requirements. The ECU still controls the same fundamental systems: direct injection, boost pressure, knock strategy, variable cam timing, throttle, and catalyst management. Tuning potential remains similar to the 156 hp version, but the same rule applies: baseline condition first, software second.",
  
