            oilSpecification: "AMG-grade MB 229.5 / MB 229.51 approved full synthetic, preferably 0W-40 or 5W-40 with short intervals",
        
            commonIssues: [
              "Carbon buildup on intake valves: The facelift engine still uses direct injection and still suffers from intake deposit formation over time. On the sharper 381 hp calibration, this affects cold-start behavior, idle quality, throttle response, and upper-rpm crispness even more noticeably than on the 360 hp version.",
              "Thermal load and heat soak: The facelift power increase came with a harder factory state of tune, so cooling-system health and intercooler efficiency became even more important. Cars that are driven hard in warm climates or maintained lazily often feel inconsistent long before they trigger obvious failure symptoms.",
              "Ignition sensitivity under boost: The 381 hp calibration demands excellent spark energy and plug condition. Worn plugs or marginal coils can cause under-load misfires, hesitation, and unstable high-rpm running, especially on tuned or heat-soaked cars.",
              "PCV / breather contamination: Once crankcase ventilation quality declines, oil vapor in the intake rises, carbon buildup accelerates, and drivability can become inconsistent. Because the facelift engine is sharper everywhere, the driver usually feels this degradation sooner.",
              "Charge-air leaks: Small pressure leaks in the boost tract or intercooler plumbing can quietly erase the stronger facelift character. The car may still feel quick, but it no longer delivers the violent midrange and sharp transient response it should.",
              "Cooling-system wear in surrounding components: The engine itself is strong, but the plastic-heavy peripheral cooling components remain exposed to repeated heat cycles. Slow leaks, thermostat issues, or heat exchanger contamination should never be ignored on a facelift CLA 45.",
              "DCT servicing neglect: The facelift model received drivetrain-related updates and shorter gearing behavior in period, making the transmission an even more active part of the package. Skipped DCT servicing quickly undermines the sharper powertrain feel and can make the car feel clumsy rather than precise."
            ],
        
            vulnerabilities: [
              "The biggest hidden vulnerability of the facelift M133.980 is that the engine code stayed the same while the operating behavior changed meaningfully. Buyers often assume a 2014 and a 2017 CLA 45 share not only the same hardware family but the same ownership profile, which is not really true. The facelift car runs a more aggressive factory tune and therefore depends even more on cooling efficiency, ignition quality, and maintenance discipline.",
              "Heat management is more important on the facelift cars than many owners realize. AMG extracted the extra 21 hp and 25 Nm without reinventing the engine code, which is impressive, but it also means the surrounding systems are working harder from the factory. Dirty radiators, weak coolant parts, tired intercooler performance, or repeated hot shut-down habits all have more consequence here than on the earlier 360 hp version.",
              "Direct injection remains an unavoidable long-term airflow vulnerability. Intake valve deposits are guaranteed with time, and the facelift engine's sharper throttle and stronger upper-range behavior make even modest carbon accumulation easier to feel from behind the wheel. In practice, this means facelift owners should think about intake cleaning as part of normal high-performance maintenance, not as a rare repair event.",
              "The 7-speed DCT is a paired-system risk that becomes more important with the facelift driveline changes. The shorter gearing and stronger output make the drivetrain feel faster and more aggressive, but they also make weak fluid condition, overdue filters, or tired clutch behavior more obvious. Engine and gearbox condition on facelift CLA 45s should always be judged together.",
              "Tuning is especially tempting on the facelift car because it already feels like a factory Stage 1 version of the early model. That encourages owners to stack extra software on top of an already hard-working package without first verifying intercooler health, plugs, coils, carbon level, and transmission condition. The result is often impressive dyno bragging and mediocre real-world reliability.",
              "The used market hides year-based nuance badly. Since the engine code did not change, many sellers present all M133 CLA 45s as essentially identical, when in reality the facelift cars have meaningful revisions in output, torque, and driveline behavior. A buyer who understands those year-specific differences is much less likely to overpay for the wrong example.",
              "Premium fuel quality is absolutely non-negotiable on the facelift engine. The sharper 381 hp calibration relies heavily on knock resistance and stable combustion, and poor fuel does more than reduce performance; it increases thermal stress and undermines the engine's long-term margin under boost."
            ],
        
