              timingType: "Chain-driven DOHC timing system. Unlike the smaller OM607, the OM651 uses a timing chain layout that better matches what many buyers expect from a Mercedes diesel, and it is generally more reassuring from a long-term ownership perspective. That said, chain drive does not mean zero maintenance concern. Oil quality, stretch symptoms, tensioner behavior, and cold-start noise still matter, especially on engines that have lived on extended service intervals or commercial-style fleet duty. In normal use the OM651 timing system is typically more confidence-inspiring than a belt-driven small diesel, but it still deserves proper monitoring rather than blind faith.",
          
              injectionType: "Common-rail direct diesel injection with Mercedes diesel calibration, here software-limited to 109 hp for entry-level/fleet use. This makes the OM651.901 an unusual package because the engine itself belongs to a more substantial diesel family than the output figure suggests. The result is a torque-rich, under-stressed feel at low and mid rpm, but also the normal modern diesel sensitivities around injectors, EGR, DPF loading, and fuel quality. Because it is detuned, the engine often feels less strained than the 1.5-liter alternative, but emissions-related maintenance remains just as important.",
          
              engineLifespan: "350,000-500,000+ km is realistic on healthy examples because the OM651 is fundamentally a tougher and more substantial engine family than the headline 109 hp output suggests. Its real-world lifespan is often determined by injector condition, cooling health, oil service quality, DPF use pattern, and transmission maintenance rather than by the strength of the base engine. In this specific low-output application, the hardware is rarely working near its real capability, which is good for durability but only if servicing has remained disciplined.",
          
              turboType: "Single turbo diesel setup tuned conservatively for fleet usability, torque delivery, and emissions compliance rather than excitement. Because the engine is software-restricted to 109 hp, the turbo system usually operates with more margin than in stronger OM651 applications. That helps drivability and durability, but only if soot control, oil quality, and boost-system sealing remain healthy.",
          
              ecuType: "Mercedes diesel ECU with software-limited output strategy. The detuned nature of this engine is one of its most interesting features, because it means the hardware package often feels stronger and more relaxed than the power number implies. Mild tuning can therefore unlock useful extra performance, but the wiser value lies in enjoying the under-stressed nature of the stock setup and keeping the diesel systems healthy.",
          
