                compression: "10.6:1",
                yearRange: "2019-2023",
            
                timingType: "Chain-driven DOHC timing system. The M282 uses a front-mounted timing chain with variable cam phasing on both the intake and exhaust camshafts. This chain is designed for the life of the engine, completely avoiding the rigid and expensive replacement intervals of a timing belt. However, its longevity is strictly tied to oil quality and maintenance frequency; extended oil intervals or chronic low oil levels will accelerate tensioner wear and chain stretch, leading to cold-start rattles and eventual timing correlation faults.",
            
                injectionType: "Direct Injection (High Pressure). This setup features centrally mounted injectors that deliver fuel directly into the combustion chamber at up to 250 bar, maximizing fuel atomization, efficiency, and low-end torque. Because the fuel does not pass over the intake valves, they are deprived of the cleaning effect of gasoline, leading to inevitable carbon buildup over time. Owners must anticipate the need for professional intake valve decarbonization (walnut blasting) around 80,000 to 100,000 km to restore idle quality and prevent misfires.",
            
                engineLifespan: "250,000+ km when meticulously maintained. The block utilizes advanced Nanoslide iron-carbon cylinder coating, which drastically reduces internal friction and cylinder wall wear over its lifespan. The mechanical core is robust, but the engine's real-world survival often depends on the longevity of its auxiliary systems, primarily the plastic thermal management module and the direct-injection high-pressure fuel pump.",
            
                turboType: "Single, electronically actuated turbocharger. The inclusion of an electronic wastegate ensures incredibly precise boost control, delivering maximum torque from just 1,620 RPM and effectively eliminating traditional turbo lag. The compact turbo operates at high temperatures and relies completely on the engine oil for cooling and lubrication, making premium synthetic oil vital for preventing bearing failure.",
            
                ecuType: "Bosch MED17 series engine management. This sophisticated ECU controls the direct injection, electronic wastegate, and variable valve timing. It is highly responsive to aftermarket tuning, allowing tuners to easily extract more boost from the turbocharger, though this must be balanced carefully against the thermal limits of the cooling system.",
            
                euroStandard: "Euro 6d-TEMP",
                maxPowerStockInternals: "200 - 215 hp (The internal rotating assembly easily supports this, but pushing beyond this limit places excessive strain on the 7G-DCT transmission clutch packs and the stock intercooler).",
                
