                yearRange: "2019-2023",
            
                timingType: "Chain-driven DOHC timing system located at the front of the engine block. The M260 utilizes a robust roller chain, but in the North American market, the factory-recommended 10,000-mile (16,000 km) oil change intervals are notoriously too long for the health of the chain tensioners. Repeatedly running old, fuel-diluted oil will cause the hydraulic tensioners to lose pressure, leading to chain slack, aggressive cold-start rattling, and eventually fatal jump-timing events. Strict adherence to 5,000-mile intervals is the only proven method to ensure the timing system outlasts the chassis.",
            
                injectionType: "Direct Injection (GDI) utilizing central piezo injectors. Operating at very high pressures, this system allows for excellent fuel atomization and cooling of the combustion chamber, which is crucial for meeting US EPA/SULEV emissions standards. However, because the fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, the intake valves receive zero detergent wash, guaranteeing severe carbon buildup over 50,000 miles. This necessitates manual walnut blasting to cure rough idle and misfires, exacerbated by varying qualities of US ethanol-blended fuels.",
            
                engineLifespan: "150,000 - 200,000+ miles (240,000 - 320,000 km), strictly dependent on proactive intervention regarding the cylinder head. The M260 has a well-documented and severe vulnerability where the exhaust valve seats wear prematurely, leading to a loss of compression and requiring a complete, highly expensive cylinder head replacement. If the cylinder head survives or has been replaced with the revised factory part, and oil changes are kept strictly to 5,000 miles, the bottom end is structurally sound enough to reach high mileage.",
            
                turboType: "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger. The twin-scroll design perfectly suits the North American driving style, providing rapid spool-up and maximum torque at very low RPMs for highway merging and city traffic. It features an electronic wastegate for highly precise boost control, though the actuator linkage can occasionally rattle or seize if exposed to heavy road salt and corrosion in northern US states.",
            
                ecuType: "Bosch MED17.7.7 engine management system. It features highly restrictive North American emissions programming (ULEV/SULEV) and advanced knock control to compensate for lower-octane US fuels (91 AKI minimum recommended). While it holds significant tuning potential, overriding the complex torque-management requests between the engine and the 7G-DCT can result in aggressive shift shocks if not calibrated correctly.",
            
                euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 3 Bin 30 / California LEV III (SULEV30)",
                maxPowerStockInternals: "260 - 280 hp. The rotating assembly is essentially identical to the higher-output CLA 250, meaning the block can easily handle a Stage 1 tune. However, the true limiting factor is the lifespan of the exhaust valves and the thermal capacity of the factory intercooler during hot North American summers.",
            
