                compression: "10.5:1",
                yearRange: "2023-present",
            
                timingType: "Chain-driven DOHC, located at the REAR of the engine (flywheel side). This represents a massive architectural shift from the older M260. Mercedes moved the timing drive to the rear to lower the front hood line for pedestrian safety and aerodynamics. While the chain itself is durable, this placement turns a standard timing chain replacement into an engine-out or transmission-out job, resulting in astronomical labor costs. Therefore, absolute perfection with oil change intervals is mandatory to prevent the chain from ever wearing out.",
            
                injectionType: "High-Pressure Direct Injection (350 Bar) with centrally located piezo injectors. The extreme fuel pressure allows for incredibly precise multi-spark and multi-injection events per stroke, optimizing the burn for Euro 6e compliance. However, because no fuel washes the intake valves, carbon buildup is still a guaranteed reality over 80,000 km, requiring physical cleaning.",
            
                engineLifespan: "250,000+ km for the mechanical core, but limited entirely by the incredibly complex electrical subsystems. The core engine block features advanced NANOSLIDE coating and is highly durable. However, the transmission-mounted 48V Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) and the intensely complicated variable thermal management module are much more likely to fail and economically total the car long before the pistons or crankshaft wear out.",
            
                turboType: "Twin-Scroll Turbocharger, positioned extremely close to the exhaust manifold. It utilizes a highly responsive electronic wastegate and works in tandem with the 48V ISG. The ISG fills the torque gap at low RPMs before the turbocharger fully spools, creating a completely seamless acceleration curve devoid of traditional turbo lag.",
            
                ecuType: "Next-generation Bosch engine management. It is vastly more complicated than previous iterations because it must simultaneously manage combustion timing, variable valve lift (CAMTRONIC), dual-circuit thermal management, and the high-voltage torque-fill handshake with the 48V ISG. Tuning this ECU requires cracking high-level encryption and carefully balancing hybrid parameters.",
            
                euroStandard: "Euro 6e",
                maxPowerStockInternals: "280 - 300 hp (Combustion limit). The NANOSLIDE cylinders and CONICSHAPE honing make the block highly efficient, but the major tuning bottleneck is the 48V ISG and dual-clutch transmission's ability to sync abnormal torque spikes. Pushing beyond Stage 1 often results in severe drivetrain judder as the electric and gas motors desynchronize.",
            
