                valves: 16,
                compression: "10.0:1",
                yearRange: "2019-2023",
            
                timingType: "Chain-driven DOHC timing system located at the front of the block. The engine utilizes a durable roller chain and hydraulic tensioners to maintain synchronization. However, the extreme heat prevalent in the Middle Eastern and South African markets severely accelerates oil viscosity breakdown, which can quickly starve the tensioners of pressure and lead to fatal timing jump if the oil is not changed every 10,000 km.",
            
                injectionType: "High-pressure Direct Injection (GDI) with central piezo injectors. Because these specific markets frequently struggle with lower-tier fuels containing high sulfur or inconsistent octane ratings, the injectors are subjected to severe stress. The lack of port injection means the intake valves receive no fuel wash, leading to rapid, hardened carbon buildup that severely impacts idle stability and airflow.",
            
                engineLifespan: "200,000 - 250,000+ km, heavily dictated by thermal management and filtration discipline. The core block is immensely strong, but survival in hot, dusty climates requires replacing air filters at double the normal frequency to prevent sand-blasting the turbocharger. If the cooling system is maintained and the common exhaust valve seat defect is avoided or repaired, the bottom end will easily outlast the chassis.",
            
                turboType: "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger. The twin-scroll exhaust manifold separates gas pulses to eliminate turbo lag, delivering peak torque at an ultra-low 1,800 RPM. In this specific detuned variant, maximum boost pressure is electronically capped to prevent pre-ignition and catastrophic heat soak when operating in 40°C+ ambient temperatures.",
            
                ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.7 engine management. This specific market ECU features a heavily modified, conservative software map that detunes the engine from 224 hp down to 211 hp. The primary objective of this calibration is aggressive knock prevention and thermal protection when the engine is subjected to poor fuel quality and extreme desert climates.",
            
