                timingType: "Chain-driven DOHC timing system located at the front of the block. The introduction of the 48V mild-hybrid system alters the timing chain's lifecycle compared to the standard model. While the Belt-driven Starter-Generator (BSG) dramatically smooths out the physical shock of engine start-ups, the sheer frequency of auto start-stop events in hybrid mode places different continuous stress on the hydraulic tensioners. Consistent 10,000 km oil changes remain absolutely paramount to keeping the tensioners fully pressurized and preventing chain stretch.",
              
                injectionType: "High-pressure Direct Injection (GDI) utilizing central piezo injectors. The injectors operate flawlessly under the complex transitions between electric coasting and combustion power, managing fuel delivery precisely during start-stop events. However, because the engine turns off frequently while coasting on the highway, the intake valves remain highly susceptible to unwashed carbon buildup, demanding professional walnut blasting by 80,000 km to cure rough idling and restore airflow.",
              
                engineLifespan: "250,000+ km for the combustion core, but the lifespan of the vehicle as an economic unit is entirely bound to the 48V electrical architecture. The internal combustion block is exceptionally robust, and by this late pre-facelift production run, the notorious exhaust valve seat defects were largely rectified by the factory. However, the 48V lithium-ion battery and the DC/DC converter are failure-prone components that can permanently brick the vehicle and cost thousands of euros to replace.",
              
                turboType: "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger, supplemented by a 48V EQ Boost Belt-driven Starter-Generator (BSG). The BSG provides an instant 150 Nm of electric torque the exact millisecond the throttle is pressed, completely masking the split-second it takes for the exhaust gases to spool the turbocharger. This integration results in an incredibly smooth, lag-free, naturally aspirated-like throttle response across the entire rev range.",
              
                ecuType: "Bosch MED 17.7.7 heavily integrated with the 48V electrical control modules. The ECU orchestrates a highly complex ballet between fuel injection, electronic wastegate actuation, and the 14 hp electrical torque fill provided by the BSG. Tuning this mild-hybrid variant is possible but requires highly specialized software to prevent the ECU and the 48V controller from desynchronizing and throwing the car into a hard limp mode.",
              
