                  "BSG Belt Snapping: Because the starter motor is now a belt-driven generator, it applies up to 150 Nm of torque directly through a rubber ribbed belt. If the tensioner weakens or the belt is neglected past 60,000 km, it will snap under load, instantly disabling the water pump, alternator, and engine starting capability.",
