                  "Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) Failure: Positioned between the engine and transmission, the ISG replaces the starter and alternator. If the ISG stator or rotor fails, the transmission must be completely separated from the engine to replace it, totaling massive repair costs out of warranty.",
                  "48V System Brick: If the 48V battery depletes or dies, the vehicle cannot be jump-started via traditional 12V means. The car becomes a 1.5-ton brick requiring dealership-level diagnostic revival and a highly expensive replacement battery.",
