                timingType: "Timing Chain system, heavily integrated into the REAR of the engine block (flywheel side). This transverse architecture utilizes a highly complex timing chain setup driving the camshafts. While designed as a 'lifetime' component, delayed oil changes or excessive stop-start city driving will cause the chain to stretch and the tensioners to fail. Because the chain is located at the back against the firewall, replacing a rattling timing chain requires dropping the entire transmission and subframe, resulting in staggering labor costs.",
            
                injectionType: "Ultra-high-pressure Common Rail Direct Injection (Bosch) operating at up to 2,050 bar. This facelift generation features highly advanced piezo injectors capable of multiple micro-injections per combustion stroke, which almost entirely eliminates traditional diesel 'clatter'. The system is incredibly reliable but absolutely intolerant of poor-quality fuel, water contamination, or delayed fuel filter replacements. The high-pressure fuel pump (HPFP) is driven by the camshaft and relies purely on diesel lubricity to survive.",
            
                engineLifespan: "350,000+ km. The OM654 is a true, purebred Mercedes-Benz masterpiece featuring an all-aluminum block paired with stepped-bowl steel pistons and Nanoslide cylinder wall coatings. This eliminates the friction and thermal expansion issues of older designs. The core block is indestructible, but the lifespan of the vehicle is usually dictated by the staggering cost of replacing the rear-mounted timing chain or servicing the incredibly complex dual-EGR emissions system at high mileage.",
            
                turboType: "Equipped with a highly responsive Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). Unlike older turbos, the OM654 features water-cooled bearing housings, drastically improving thermal stability and preventing oil coking after hot shutdowns. It spools almost instantly, providing the full 320 Nm of torque very low in the rev range. It is highly robust if the air filter is kept clean and the 0W-20 oil is changed frequently.",
            
                ecuType: "Bosch MD1 Engine Management with updated emissions software for the facelift generation. The ECU controls an incredibly complex exhaust aftertreatment sequence, utilizing both High-Pressure and Low-Pressure EGR circuits, an SCR-coated DPF (sDPF), and an underbody SCR catalyst. Because this 150 hp version is literally the exact same 2.0L hardware as the 190 hp variant, the ECU is artificially capping the engine's potential, making it a legendary platform for aftermarket tuning.",
            
